@CLI_TOOL_NAME@ for Debian

This package ships install-time provisioning for per-user @CLI_TOOL_NAME@ sandbox accounts.

For an end user <u>, provisioning creates:

- system user: @CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>
- private group: @CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>
- shared group: @CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>-shared
- /home/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>/shared (setgid) workspace root
- sudoers wrapper for running a hardened command as @CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>

User enrollment

Provision your account:

  sudo /usr/libexec/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-provision-user <username>

Then re-login (or restart your session) so new processes get the new group membership.

Go toolchain

This repository uses a Go toolchain directive (go1.24.12) in go.mod.
If your distro's golang-go is older than the required version, you can install
a newer Go from https://go.dev/dl/ (or use a compatible backport), then rebuild.
